- JS findings: no app-specific `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` (only React/Radix internals); `.innerHTML` only libraries; no `eval`/`new Function`; no `srcdoc`. React escaping → DOM XSS unlikely. `picture` avatar posted as JSON `{picture: dataURL}` and rendered via `<img src>` → stored XSS unlikely.
- Redirect validation: `AC()` allows only hostnames whose last 2 labels ∈ [`ubnt.com`,`ui.com`,`uisp.com`] and protocol http/https; `qpe()` requires `innerRedirect` start with `/`, not `//`, no `\`, and match allowed route list `Bpe`. `redirect` used in `window.location.replace(...)` after login/logout → no arbitrary-domain open redirect found.
